@startuml

title Solana Trusted Notary Sequence Diagram

== Initialization Phase ==
autonumber “<b>(I##)”
box "Program Maintainer" 
actor "R3 Maintainer" as R3
end box
box "Solana Cluster" #lightblue
participant "Solana Notary Program" as SNP
database "Solana Cluster (PDA Storage)" as SC
end box

note over R3,SNP
Program deployed and initialized by R3 (single admin).
end note
R3 -> SNP: <color brown>**DF_STN_INIT_PROGRAM**</color> \n Initialize Notary Program
note right of SNP
Initialization steps:
- Set initial parameters.
- Register administrator accounts as
 PDA (caller public key).
- Authorize a Notary Pubkey
end note

== Notarisation Phase ==
autonumber “<b>(N##)”
box "Corda Participant" #pink 
actor CordaParticipant as CP
end box

box "Corda Notary Node" #LightGreen
participant "Corda Notary Node (Solana Integrated)" as CNN
end box

box "Solana Cluster" #lightblue
participant "Solana Notary Program" as SNP
database "Solana Cluster (PDA Storage)" as SC
end box

CP -> CNN: <color green>**DF_STN_SUBMIT_REQUEST**</color> \n Submit notarisation request (Corda transaction parameters)
CNN -> CNN: <color green>**DF_STN_VALIDATE_REQUEST**</color> \n Validate notarisation request (TimeWindow, Transaction ID, etc.)

alt REQUEST NOT VALID
    CNN -> CP: <color brown>**DF_STN_RETURN_FAILURE**</color> \n Return failure (invalid request)
else REQUEST SYNTAX VALID
    CNN -> SNP: <color green>**DF_STN_INVOKE_COMMIT**</color> \n Invoke `commit` instruction with parameters
    note right of SNP
      See: [[https://github.com/corda/enterprise/blob/e8b0346eae512a178c5316bfab74efdfe28ee645/solana-aggregator/notary-program/programs/corda-notary/src/commit.rs commit.rs]]
    end note
    note right of SNP
      RFI: what is remaining_accounts?
    end note
    SNP -> SNP: <color green>**DF_STN_VERIFY_ACCOUNT_COUNT**</color> \n Verify number of accounts passed in
    SNP -> SC: <color green>**DF_STN_CHECK_OUTPUT_ACCOUNT**</color> \n Retrieve output account and check if unused

    alt Output Account Already Used
        SNP -> CNN: <color brown>**DF_STN_RETURN_FAILURE**</color> \n Return failure (resubmission detected)
        CNN -> CP: <color brown>**DF_STN_NOTIFY_RESULT**</color> \n Notify notarisation result (Resubmission failure)
        break
        end
    else Output Account New
        SNP -> SC: <color green>**DF_STN_CREATE_OUTPUT_ACCOUNT**</color> \n Create and initialize output account with transaction data
        SNP -> SNP: <color green>**DF_STN_PROCESS_INPUTS_REFERENCES**</color> \n Process inputs and references

        loop For each group in inputs and references
            SNP -> SC: <color green>**DF_STN_RETRIEVE_STATE_ACCOUNT**</color> \n Retrieve or create state account
            loop For each input index
                SNP -> SC: <color green>**DF_STN_CHECK_UNSPENT_BIT**</color> \n Verify bit is set (unspent)
                alt Unspent Bit is not set (DOUBLE SPEND)
                    SNP -> CNN: <color brown>**DF_STN_RETURN_FAILURE**</color> \n Return failure (Already consumed)
                    CNN -> CP: <color brown>**DF_STN_NOTIFY_RESULT**</color> \n Notify notarisation result (Already consumed)
                    break
                    end
                else Unspent Bit is set (FIRST SPEND)
                    SNP -> SC: <color green>**DF_STN_CLEAR_UNSPENT_BIT**</color> \n Clear bit (mark as spent)
                 
                end
            loop For each reference index
                SNP -> SC: <color green>**DF_STN_VERIFY_REFERENCE_BIT**</color> \n Verify bit is set (valid reference)
     
            end
        end

        SNP -> SC: <color green>**DF_STN_UPDATE_SOL_STATES**</color> \n Update stateRefs (Mark input states as spent, output states as unspent)
        SNP -> CNN: <color green>**DF_STN_RETURN_SUCCESS**</color> \n Return TX SUCCESS
        CNN -> CP: <color green>**DF_STN_NOTIFY_RESULT**</color> \n Notify notarisation result (SUCCESS)
    end
end

@enduml
